  "implemented_behavior": [
    "R10K has a distinct orchestrator state, native entry receipts and partial recovery phase. Partial entry retains zero canonical initialization and confirmation counts and preserves the original passive timeout and kick energy epoch.",
    "The actual candidate worker selects these hooks only for the explicitly named R10K route. It applies unchanged native V20/V7 commands through the real motor applier, binds task identity to the applied command and model before sampling, and verifies the binding against its current partial memory before native reads.",
    "Partial processing retains exact requests, responses, source observations and prior memory. Native completion requires 60 standing samples. The final partial observation stays retained while its model source tag is removed before fresh walking.",
    "The genuine-prone branch installs only its actual canonical handoff under the prospective 360-command standing profile and retains its genuine 12-sample confirmation. The unselected worker continues its original state machine and source path."
  ],
